title: Add optional header pruning

doc:
- audience: [Node Dev, Node Operator]
  description: |-
    Adds an opt-in `--enable-header-pruning` node flag. When used together with a numeric
    `--blocks-pruning N`, the headers (and their key-lookup entries) of pruned finalized blocks
    are removed from the database as well, instead of being kept forever. This bounds the
    otherwise unbounded, monotonic header-chain growth on fully-pruned validator/authoring nodes.

    Headers required for warp sync (blocks retained by a `PruningFilter`, e.g. GRANDPA authority
    set changes) and pinned blocks are never pruned. The flag is a no-op in archive modes.

    NOTE: a node started with `--enable-header-pruning` can no longer answer queries for pruned
    historical headers and must not be used as an archive or full-sync source.

    For downstream code constructing the affected structs directly, new fields default to `false`
    (previous behavior, headers kept):
    - `sc_client_db::DatabaseSettings` gains a `header_pruning: bool` field.
    - `sc_service::Configuration` gains a `header_pruning: bool` field.
    - `sc_cli::PruningParams` gains an `enable_header_pruning: bool` field.
    - `sc_cli::CliConfiguration` gains a `header_pruning()` method (default impl reads it from
      `PruningParams`).

crates:
- name: sc-client-db
  bump: major
- name: sc-service
  bump: major
- name: sc-cli
  bump: major
- name: frame-benchmarking-cli
  bump: patch
